00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:05.430 align:start position:0%
maria dolores mercado has been coming to  the church of baklaran in the capital  manila  since she was a little girl but on the  holiest day of the christian calendar  this is as far as she's allowed to go as  in many countries  places of worship are seen as potential  hubs  for spreading coronavirus so for now  attending mass  is different for me this is enough for  now  that i am able to hear mass outside the  church his words  give me strength my faith is my guide  the church of baklaran has long been the  refuge for the faithful  who come from the poorest sector of  society  but public easter gatherings have been  restricted for a second consecutive year  raising concerns from many catholics  here  that the pandemic may have permanently  altered the ways  of worship the philippines has seen a  steep rise in corona virus cases since  february  prompting the government to impose  another round of lockdown  in manila and nearby provinces but  in recent days at least one out of four  filipinos who have been tested  have turned out positive with  coronavirus  so this priest has been left with no  choice but to preach in an empty church  although it could be watched online he  called for a moment of silence to  remember the thousands who have died  from the pandemic  sending a message of comfort to those  who are grieving  in another part of manila father flavi  villanueva runs a center for the poor  and homeless he talks about redemption  in the critical role the church can play  in society  especially when society fails to respond  appropriately  competently and justly to the needs of  the people  the church cannot remain silent it will  always serve as  a conscience of those brazen  people the church will always remain as  a light  to those dampened by their hopes  kneeling before a homeless man a  reformed drug user  a lawyer and a journalist father flabby  says  they represent those who have been  persecuted by the government  he offers a message of hope but for many  here the shadow of death  still lingers though the faithful say  they remain  fervent in their prayers christ they say  has been resurrected  and they hope filipinos will soon rise  from their sufferings  too jamal lindogan al jazeera manila
 

